<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ilkhanate</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ilkhanid, Ilkhanids</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ilkhanate was a Mongol state founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hulagu-khan">Hulagu Khan</a> in the mid-thirteenth century, ruling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> and neighbouring lands. Its rulers later converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>, and under Ghazan carried out major reforms. It has its own profile on the site, was a rival of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a>, and was one of the successor khanates of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ilkhanate.jpg" alt="Ilkhanate" width="320" height="204" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Historical_Atlas_of_Iran_-_Plate_No._17_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
